---
import { CONTRIBUTING_URL, DEMO_URL, NEW_ISSUE_URL, SELF_HOST_URL } from '../consts';
---

<section id="faq">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal="up">
      FAQ
    </p>
    <h2 data-reveal="up" style="--reveal-delay: 0.08s">
      Common <span class="accent">questions</span>
    </h2>
    <!-- Plain <details>: opens and closes with no script, and every answer is
         in the HTML for search engines and find-in-page. -->
    <div class="questions" data-reveal>
      <details style="--i: 0">
        <summary>What does it cost?</summary>
        <p>
          Nothing. Balances is open source under AGPL-3.0. You run it on your own server, and a
          small one is enough: 1&nbsp;GB of memory and one CPU.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details style="--i: 1">
        <summary>Is there a hosted version I can sign up for?</summary>
        <p>
          No. Balances only runs where you install it. The{' '}
          <a href={DEMO_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            live demo
          </a>{' '}
          is a shared account that resets every night, so it’s for looking around, not for your real
          numbers.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details style="--i: 2">
        <summary>What do I need to run it?</summary>
        <p>
          A machine with Docker and Docker Compose. You download two files, set a few values in{' '}
          <code>.env</code>, and run <code>docker compose up</code>. People can sign in with Google,
          or you can turn on email and password accounts and skip Google entirely. The{' '}
          <a href={SELF_HOST_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            self-hosting guide
          </a>{' '}
          covers HTTPS, upgrades and backups.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details style="--i: 3">
        <summary>Does it connect to my bank?</summary>
        <p>
          No, and it never asks for your bank login. You read the month-end balance off the
          statement and type it in. Nothing is scraped and nothing syncs.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details style="--i: 4">
        <summary>Can my partner use it too?</summary>
        <p>
          Yes. A household can have more than one member. You invite them, and everyone in the
          household sees and edits the same positions.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details style="--i: 5">
        <summary>What if I miss a month?</summary>
        <p>
          Nothing breaks. Each position keeps its last balance until you enter a new one, and
          Balances lists the positions that are behind so you can catch up.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details style="--i: 6">
        <summary>Can I track more than one currency?</summary>
        <p>
          Yes, once you turn multi-currency on. Each position keeps its own currency. You enter a
          month-end exchange rate, and Balances converts everything to your household’s reporting
          currency.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details style="--i: 7">
        <summary>Can I contribute?</summary>
        <p>
          Yes. Bug reports, fixes and features go through GitHub. For anything bigger than a typo,{' '}
          <a href={NEW_ISSUE_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            open an issue
          </a>{' '}
          first so the approach can be agreed before anyone writes code. The{' '}
          <a href={CONTRIBUTING_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            contributing guide
          </a>{' '}
          covers setup and how a change gets merged.
        </p>
        <p>
          Balances ships in English and Bahasa Indonesia. If you’d like to add a language, open an
          issue to start the conversation.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  section {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .container {
    padding-block: var(--section-pad-top) 4rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--secondary-foreground);
  }

  /* One reading column, narrower than the page, so answers keep a
     comfortable line length. */
  .questions {
    max-width: 46rem;
    margin: 2.5rem auto 0;
    text-align: left;
  }

  details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  details:first-child {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  summary {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding-block: 1.125rem;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    color: var(--secondary-foreground);
    text-wrap: balance;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
  }

  summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  /* A brass plus that turns into a minus when open: the vertical stroke is a
     second gradient that folds away. */
  summary::after {
    content: '';
    flex: none;
    width: 0.75rem;
    height: 0.75rem;
    background:
      linear-gradient(var(--primary), var(--primary)) center / 100% 1.5px no-repeat,
      linear-gradient(var(--primary), var(--primary)) center / 1.5px 100% no-repeat;
    transition: background-size 0.2s ease;
  }

  details[open] summary::after {
    background-size:
      100% 1.5px,
      1.5px 0;
  }

  summary:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--ring);
    outline-offset: 2px;
    border-radius: 0.25rem;
  }

  details p {
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
  }

  details p + p {
    margin-top: -0.5rem;
  }

  code {
    font-size: 0.9375em;
    color: var(--secondary-foreground);
  }

  /* Motion (paused until in view; see global.css): rows stagger up. */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    details {
      animation: reveal-up 0.6s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.7, 0.2, 1) both;
      animation-delay: calc(var(--i) * 0.05s);
    }
  }
</style>
